  summary: "Replace non-overlapping matches using a pure function from each RegexMatch to replacement text, in source order.",
  taskTitle: "Build replacement text from an optional capture",
  purpose: "Use replaceAllWith when a replacement depends on what matched. Here x12 becomes [12], while x with no digits becomes [absent]. Text outside matches is retained.",
  setup: "replacement is an ordinary function taking a RegexMatch and returning String. replaceAllWith receives the compiled Regex, that function, and the input in order. x([0-9]+)? has one optional capturing group.",
  after: [
    "compile returns Right pattern for a reusable Regex or Left error for an invalid pattern. match chooses a branch and names the value inside it. The backtick error message inserts error.offset at ${error.offset}; that offset counts UTF-8 bytes from zero.",
    "captures excludes group 0, so arrays.get 0 reads the first capturing group. The lookup itself returns Maybe: Just (Just capture) means the slot exists and matched, Just Nothing means it exists but did not match, and Nothing means the slot is absent. The code returns brackets around capture.text or an explicit fallback.",
    "The three matches are processed from left to right. Input with no x is unchanged; empty input stays empty for this pattern. The callback returns text rather than performing output. Only println in main prints.",
    "pub effect fn main is the program entry. do runs the println output steps in order. Calls separate arguments with spaces. show converts a value to display text; True/False are the Seseragi Boolean spellings."
  ],
  comparisonBefore: "JavaScript String.replace also accepts a callback. Here its arguments are the whole match and the first capture, represented as string | undefined. An explicit undefined check preserves any empty string that a participating capture could return.",
  comparisonAfter: "The demonstrated outputs agree. JavaScript provides separate callback arguments; Seseragi provides one RegexMatch record with text, byte span, an Array of optional captures and named captures. Returned replacement text is literal in both callback forms.",
  details: [
    "The callback runs once per selected match in source order. It must be a String-returning ordinary function; an Effect-returning output operation does not have that type. Use match fields to compute text and perform I/O separately.",
    "The Regex and original input are unchanged. Inserted replacement text is not matched again. Empty-match advancement follows findAll: one scalar after an empty match, including the terminal empty match before stopping."
